1. Purpose

Slice is source-available software. Its source code is published so that people can use it, learn from it, change it for themselves, and help improve it. This license grants those freedoms while keeping the right to sell or commercially redistribute Slice with the Licensor.

Slice is not open source software as defined by the Open Source Initiative, because this license restricts commercial redistribution.


2. Definitions

- “Licensor” means rit3zh, the copyright holder of Slice.
- “Software” means Slice, including its source code, compiled applications, documentation and other files published in the official repository.
- “You” means the individual or entity exercising the rights granted by this license.
- “Modified Version” means any work that contains the Software, or a substantial part of it, with changes.
- “Distribute” means to make the Software or a Modified Version available to anyone else, by any means.
- “Commercial” means intended for, or directed toward, payment, commercial advantage or monetary compensation, including through sales, subscriptions, advertising or bundling with a paid product or service.


3. Personal and professional use

You may download, install and run the Software, free of charge, on any device you own or control.

This includes using the Software at work, inside a company or organization, and to make videos for paid work. The restrictions in sections 7 to 9 apply to distributing the Software itself, not to using it.

Recordings, videos and other content you create with the Software belong to you. This license places no restrictions on how you use them.


4. Inspecting and cloning the source

You may view, download, clone and fork the source code from the official repository, build it yourself, and study how it works.


5. Modifications

You may modify the Software and run your Modified Version for your own use.

You may share the source code of a Modified Version for free, for example as a public fork of the official repository, as long as you:

- keep this license and the copyright notice with it;
- clearly mark it as modified and unofficial, and say what you changed; and
- do not charge for it or use it for a Commercial purpose.

Distributing a Modified Version commercially is not permitted unless the Licensor has given you written permission under section 12.


6. Contributions

You may propose changes to the Software by opening issues and submitting pull requests to the official repository.

By submitting a contribution, you confirm that you have the right to submit it, and you grant the Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, modify and distribute that contribution as part of the Software under this license or any later license the Licensor chooses.

You keep the copyright in your contribution. Submitting a pull request does not transfer ownership of any code to you or to the Licensor beyond the contribution itself, and gives you no rights in other parts of the Software beyond those this license already grants.

How to contribute is described in CONTRIBUTING.md in the official repository.


7. No commercial redistribution

You may not Distribute the Software, or a Modified Version, for a Commercial purpose. This includes publishing it in a paid app store listing, bundling it with a paid product or service, or offering it behind a paywall or subscription.


8. No resale as a standalone application

You may not sell, license, rent or otherwise charge for the Software or a Modified Version as a standalone application, whether as source code or as a compiled binary.


9. No rebranding as a competing product

You may not rename or rebrand the Software or a Modified Version and offer it to others as your own screen recording or video editing product, whether or not you charge for it.


10. Ownership and attribution

The Licensor keeps all copyright and other rights in the Software that this license does not expressly grant. This license does not grant any right to use the Slice name, icon or other marks, except to accurately say where the Software comes from.

You must keep this license and the copyright notice with every copy of the Software and every Modified Version.


11. Third-party components

Some parts of the Software were made by others and are under their own licenses. This license does not apply to them; their own licenses do, and they take precedence for those files.

- FluidAudio: Runs Parakeet transcription on the Neural Engine. Apache License 2.0. https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio
- SmoothGradient: Smooth gradient interpolation, by Ramon Torres. MIT License. https://github.com/raymondjavaxx/SmoothGradient
- BorderBeamKit: The capture bar's animated border, a SwiftUI port of border-beam by Jakub Antalik. Credited to the original author. https://beam.jakubantalik.com
- Sparkle: In-app updates from Slice's GitHub releases. MIT License. https://github.com/sparkle-project/Sparkle
- Safari mockup: The browser window drawn around screen recordings, after the Safari component in Magic UI. MIT License. https://github.com/magicuidesign/magicui
- 3D device models: The iPhones and MacBook in the 3D editor, by the Sketchfab artists named in the credits. CC BY 4.0, except the iPhone 18 Pro Max (Sketchfab Standard). https://github.com/rit3zh/slice/blob/main/Sources/SliceCore/Resources/Models/CREDITS.txt
- Keyboard sound packs: Cherry MX Blue (Hai Nguyen) and Holy Panda (Thomas Lai) keystroke sounds. MIT License. https://github.com/rit3zh/slice/tree/main/Sources/SliceCore/Resources/Sounds/Keyboards
- Apex Pro sound pack: Keystroke sounds. GNU GPL 3.0. https://github.com/rit3zh/slice/tree/main/Sources/SliceCore/Resources/Sounds/Keyboards/apex-pro
- DeepFilterNet3: Voice enhancement. Downloaded on request, not bundled. MIT or Apache License 2.0. https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet
- Parakeet Ultra 0.6B: Transcription model. Downloaded on request, not bundled. CC BY 4.0. https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/parakeet-ultra-coreml

Apple, iPhone, Mac and macOS are trademarks of Apple Inc. Slice is an independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Apple.


